      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks problematic. When we use `std::move` we indicate to the compiler that we will never use the moved-from object again, so it can do whatever it wants with it, but here we will in fact use it again on the next call to `getEngineConfig`. This problem would become more clear if we declare `returnEngCfg` as `static const`, which it really should be—in that case use of `std::move` will become syntactically incorrect.\n\nSo, please make `returnEngCfg` a constant, and remove `std::move`. A copy is unavoidable in this scenario, and it\u0027s OK. It\u0027s still far more cheaper to copy this object instead of re-creating it via deserialization.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "9db350f37e7a405543175d8191f815c9ba1c6199",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
